D. A random walk inward? With the number left to chance the changes of the ring's mean from one annulus to the next should be independent. Correlation between successive changes, annuli 0.2 to 0.8:
   n =   100000: mean of the 11 correlations +0.035 (one over the root of the number of clouds is 0.016); least +0.019, greatest +0.063. An annulus has a width, and the mean over it of a walk with independent steps gives +0.060
   n =  1000000: mean of the 11 correlations +0.063 (one over the root of the number of clouds is 0.022); least +0.022, greatest +0.134. An annulus has a width, and the mean over it of a walk with independent steps gives +0.060
   n = 10000000: mean of the 11 correlations +0.041 (one over the root of the number of clouds is 0.071); least -0.045, greatest +0.117. An annulus has a width, and the mean over it of a walk with independent steps gives +0.060

